From 00a445d733086da52c6b905fa287f0ea64a85938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 16:39:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: sched: sch_cake: use flow_hash_from_keys_small() for
 host accounting

cake_hash() computes three flow_keys hashes per packet on the
enqueue path: one main hash (flow_hash) used as the queue index,
plus two synthesised host_keys hashes (dsthost_hash and
srchost_hash) used for dual-source-host fair queueing.

The two host_keys hashes are internal to sch_cake's host-load
accounting; their values are used as keys into cake's own
hosts[] table and are never compared against skb->hash or any
other externally-derived hash. Switching them to
flow_hash_from_keys_small() shaves the siphash region from
~40 B (IPv4) or ~64 B (IPv6) down to 16 B / 40 B respectively,
roughly halving the per-hash cycle cost on IPv4.

The main flow_hash at the end of the switch is unchanged
because it ends up as the cake-internal queue index. Future
work could switch it too, but keeping the change minimal makes
this patch easy to review in isolation.

Per-packet saving (modeled from microbench on AMD Zen 2):
roughly 80 cycles per packet (two hashes saving ~40 cycles
each), or ~25 ns/pkt at 3 GHz. On a 10 Gb/s link saturating
the queue this compounds to noticeable CPU saving at the
queue-management layer.

The new helper falls back to flow_hash_from_keys() for
non-IPv4/IPv6 address types, but cake's default case zeros
both host hashes anyway, so the fallback path is never taken
from cake's call sites.

Signed-off-by: Dave Seddon <dave.seddon.ca@gmail.com>
---
 net/sched/sch_cake.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/sched/sch_cake.c b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
index a3c185505afc..47932e355ded 100644
--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -753,20 +753,20 @@ static u32 cake_hash(struct cake_tin_data *q, const struct sk_buff *skb,
 	switch (host_keys.control.addr_type) {
 	case FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV4_ADDRS:
 		host_keys.addrs.v4addrs.src = 0;
-		dsthost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys(&host_keys);
+		dsthost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys_small(&host_keys);
 		host_keys.addrs.v4addrs.src = keys.addrs.v4addrs.src;
 		host_keys.addrs.v4addrs.dst = 0;
-		srchost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys(&host_keys);
+		srchost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys_small(&host_keys);
 		break;
 
 	case FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_IPV6_ADDRS:
 		memset(&host_keys.addrs.v6addrs.src, 0,
 		       sizeof(host_keys.addrs.v6addrs.src));
-		dsthost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys(&host_keys);
+		dsthost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys_small(&host_keys);
 		host_keys.addrs.v6addrs.src = keys.addrs.v6addrs.src;
 		memset(&host_keys.addrs.v6addrs.dst, 0,
 		       sizeof(host_keys.addrs.v6addrs.dst));
-		srchost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys(&host_keys);
+		srchost_hash = flow_hash_from_keys_small(&host_keys);
 		break;
 
 	default:
